<title>USA: Outgoing FDA chief cites speedier drug approvals.</title>
<headline>Outgoing FDA chief cites speedier drug approvals.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Outgoing Food and Drug Administration chief David Kessler on Tuesday rejected criticisms the agency was lagging in reviewing new products and approving them for marketing.</p>
<p>Kessler told the Food and Drug Law Institute that approval times for new drugs and for new uses for old drugs had dropped steadily in recent years.  And new medical devices were also being made available quicker.</p>
<p>&quot;All of this means that American patients are getting the medications they need faster and more efficiently,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
